* powerape.pkg -- package-description file for the powerape Stata port
* Install:  net install powerape, from("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jespernwulff/powerape-stata/main/")
* Extras:   net get powerape, from(...)   (ancillary: showcase.do, a guided tour, and build.do)
* Then:     mata: mata mlib index
v 3
d 'POWERAPE': module for power analysis for average partial effects (APE) and average interaction effects (AIE)
d
d powerape is a Stata port of the R package powerape (version 1.11.3,
d https://github.com/jespernwulff/powerape): simulation-based power analysis
d in which the effect size of interest is the average partial effect or the
d average interaction effect of a probit or logit model, stated in probability
d points. The package calibrates the data-generating process (baseline rate
d plus nuisance signal), inverts the target into coefficients, checks
d feasibility, and computes power for three confidence-interval claims
d (detect / minimum-effect / equivalence), power curves, required sample
d sizes with a confirmation stage, minimum detectable effects, robustness
d sweeps with n_max, citable power statements, and justified error rates.
d Routes: parametric covariates, covariates resampled from pilot data, a
d fitted probit/logit pilot model, correlated random effects panel probit,
d and an endogenous focal variable (control-function probit, cfprobit).
d
d Requirements: Stata 16 or later (frames). The default engine(stata) on the
d IV route calls cfprobit (Stata 18 or later); engine(mata) covers every route
d on Stata 16 or later. Tested on StataNow 19.5 (update 14 Oct 2026) only. The
d shipped Mata library lpowerape.mlib was compiled by StataNow 19.5; a Mata
d library compiled by a newer Stata may not load in an older one, so on Stata
d 16-18 rebuild it from the .mata sources (net get powerape, then do build.do)
d and run mata: mata mlib index. After installing, run -powerape version- to
d check that the ado-file and the Mata library match.
d
d Version 0.1.3 (17 October 2026): panel designs calibrate about as fast as
d in the R package (a panel dgp, setape or trueape at the default nint(1e5)
d took about a minute and now takes one to three seconds); every result is
d identical to 0.1.2.
d
d Version 0.1.2 (16 October 2026): every simulation command prints a line
d "fit: ..." naming who fitted the simulated studies (for example probit via
d engine(stata), effects(closed), or Mata engine (Fisher scoring)) and stores
d it in r(fit), r(engine) and r(effects).
d
d KW: power analysis
d KW: sample size
d KW: average partial effect
d KW: average marginal effect
d KW: interaction effect
d KW: probit
d KW: logit
d KW: control function
d KW: simulation
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261017
d
d Author: Jesper N. Wulff, Aarhus University
d Support: https://github.com/jespernwulff/powerape-stata/issues
d Documentation, in Stata and R: https://jespernwulff.github.io/powerape/
d
